---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import SlugGenerator from '../../components/SlugGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Slug Generator"
  description="Convert any text into a clean, URL-friendly slug — instantly, with hyphen or underscore separators."
>
  <SlugGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>What a slug is and why it matters</h2>
  <p>
    A slug is the URL-friendly version of a title — lowercase, no special
    characters, words separated by hyphens. Clean slugs matter for SEO,
    readability, and avoiding broken links caused by spaces or special
    characters in URLs.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this tool</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Type or paste your title/text.</li>
    <li>Choose a separator (hyphen is the SEO-standard choice).</li>
    <li>Click the result to copy it.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Hyphen or underscore?</strong> Hyphens are the standard for SEO
    — Google treats hyphens as word separators but treats underscores as
    joining words together, which can hurt keyword matching.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does this handle accented characters?</strong> Yes — accented
    letters (like é or ñ) are converted to their closest plain-ASCII
    equivalent automatically.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
